// The contributors of a head aggregate (BENCH-135 "3 and 1 contributors"; the property of the aggregate-provenance
// test in Molly's provenance suite, R06 §12.6), written for this corpus: tally(k, "x", 3) counts the three readings
// 5, 6 and 7 of sensor x, and tally(k, "y", 1) the single reading 9 of sensor y, so they have 3 and 1 contributors.
// The readings pass through the derived relation `seen`, so the contributors are derived goals. Blossom golden
// corpus, re-derived (derived = true); see ../../README.md.

seen(K, Sensor, V) :- reading(K, Sensor, V);
tally(K, Sensor, count<V>) :- seen(K, Sensor, V);

reading("k", "x", 5)@1;
reading("k", "x", 6)@1;
reading("k", "x", 7)@1;
reading("k", "y", 9)@1;
